LANDING PR for story #634, slice A (decision 0083: an adopter's Brokkr lives in one .brokkr/ folder). This slice builds folder DISCOVERY, the DEFAULTS that follow from it, and the OLD-LAYOUT REFUSALS. Slice B, later, makes init write the folder and doctor check it. The operator ruled on #634 on 2026-10-13, settling 0083's open points; follow these rulings over any contrary text in 0083:
1. A recipe library (recipes/*/bundle.json) is EXEMPT from the old-layout refusal: a library keeps its layout, a tracked root bundle.json beside recipes/ included.
2. init reads and writes one path: the folder it creates.
3. Doctor's folder line uses the report's usual status column.
4. The compile-derived move list is dropped: the old-layout refusal lists the state moves only.

The branch story-634-slice-a ends at 52fcea71. Its history in brief:
- 290e80fd: the slice.
- Fix rounds:
  - 634b (a5be0739);
  - 634c (b3132bc2);
  - 634i (2312461d: places.rs is the ONE judgement of a workspace's layout);
  - 634j (87809929: the physical walk);
  - 634k (83251f2d, beb31337, f521529a: MapSource::now's Ambient arm, folder_bundle by Kind, typed git reads, enum Move and its executed property table).
- The controller's commits: fff310e0 (Sparse), merges of main, the clone baseline and cli.md, and the coverage and complexity fixes.
- The fourth landing (landing-pr-for-story-634-slice-a-0959df12) spent three implement rounds (cea25b8f, 7832ced6, 6d46af6a) on link spellings inside .forge. No round found a security residual. The operator then ruled, on 2026-10-14 (option 1, recorded on #634): ANY symbolic link in or under .forge, and a .forge that is itself a link, makes the old-layout refusal list NO moves and refuse by name ("move it yourself"), at any depth. Brokkr stops resolving links in the move list. That landing was stopped under the ruling.
- ff0ec09b (fix round 634m, fix-round-634m-for-story-634-sli-ffe0244f; its panel and chief ruled CLEAN on the first review; host exact coverage green):
  - state_moves decides no_link(root/.forge) first, before Forge::at and any git question. It walks .forge and every entry at every depth by symlink_metadata (places::entry), never follows a link, and refuses FolderError::Link { path }, naming the first link in sorted walk order, in the ruling's words. An unreadable entry refuses as Unreadable.
  - Deleted as unreachable: links.rs, ForgeHoldsRoot, LinkedTracked, Link(LinkRefusal), tracked::Index, Forge::Link and Forge::linked, Move::Unlink with its note and `rm .forge`, and the ignore file's link case.
  - The property table has four Link refusal rows (.forge itself, .forge/.gitignore, .forge/forge.db, .forge/results/run/out), each asserting no file moved and nothing was created.
  - Old-layout DETECTION is unchanged: a linked .forge is still an old layout; only the list refuses.
  - Net -470 lines.
- 346ded08 (the controller's): a clean merge of origin/main 40426a50 (#668, #669).
- 52fcea71 (the controller's): #669 lowered bundle.rs's file-lines baseline to 7152, and the merged file stood at 7156. bundle.rs's private unpinned_top_level only forwarded to places::unpinned_top_level, so it went, and its three callers name the places rule. bundle.rs is now 7142 lines, with no behaviour change.
Host exact coverage is green on ff0ec09b. The controller reruns it, with the lints, after this landing.

Every review position, panel member or chief, is READ-ONLY: it changes no tracked file and makes no commit, whatever this text asks below. It reports each finding. Only the implement phase fixes a finding the review returns.

Judge:
1. The operator's ruling of 2026-10-14 is built as stated, and only it:
   - any symbolic link at or under .forge, at any depth, .forge itself included, refuses by name before any move is listed and before any git question;
   - nothing in the list builder still resolves or follows a link;
   - the deletions remove exactly what the rule made unreachable;
   - detection of an old layout is unchanged.
   Reproduce on the HEAD binary: a .forge that is a link, and a link at each depth under it. Each refuses in the ruling's words, with no file moved and nothing created.
2. The move lists. brokkr_folder::the_listed_moves_empty_every_forge executes every list it builds, and covers every arm of enum Move and every shape the builder handles without a link. A list that, executed, leaves .forge standing or loses an entry is a finding. A shape git cannot complete (index or work-tree changes, a sparse checkout, a submodule, an unreadable git) must refuse by name before listing.
3. ONE judgement. Every layout fact comes from places.rs, with no second derivation, CLI or dispatch:
   - the physical walk, the nested refusal, the root .brokkr entry, the library mark, the old layouts, the no-place rule with its --db escape, and the default map's presence;
   - folder_bundle's judgement by Kind;
   - MapSource::now's Unmapped and Ambient arms.
   Reproduce the earlier rounds' shapes on the HEAD binary:
   - an unreadable recipes/;
   - a .brokkr/ removed, or nested, after `queue add`;
   - a workspace moved behind a symlink;
   - a directory or dangling link at the default map;
   - an Ambient entry whose map moved;
   - a library recipe named .brokkr.
   Each must refuse by name, or be held, with nothing created.
4. Discovery and precedence follow 0083 ruling 2 as the operator's ruling 1 amends it. A library behaves exactly as today:
   - in Brokkr's own checkout and in a temp library, --db/--bundle behave as before;
   - a library recipe pins a top-level state/;
   - the capability_broker suite passes unedited.
   In a fresh git repo with a hand-planted .brokkr/, a fake-driver `brokkr run --feature x` from a subdirectory with no flags writes .brokkr/state/forge.db and .brokkr/state/results/, and leaves `git status` clean apart from .brokkr/.
5. Scope. No file of decision 0065 slice two's changes except verbs/readouts.rs's one message, and nothing under contracts/, fixtures/, policy/phase-machine.json or reference/. QueuedLaunch gains no field. Every merge changes neither side, and 52fcea71 changes no behaviour.
6. The Ruling line's items are complete and true, for the PR:
   - the public API changes: brokkr-runtime's places module as it now stands, admission's Difference::Map { was, now }, and brokkr-cli's removal of DEFAULT_DB and DEFAULT_SECRETS;
   - ruling 1 read over 0083 ruling 2's step order;
   - the state skip scoped to the folder bundle;
   - ledger --repo's unconditional --db escape;
   - places::folder refusing a non-directory .brokkr before the library mark is consulted;
   - compile and recipes skipping the old-layout refusal until slice B;
   - the operator's link ruling, which narrows 0083 ruling 4's move-list sentence (name it), with an addendum owed;
   - the controller's clone baseline refresh;
   - main sits between slices: until slice B, init still writes the root layout, which a run then refuses.
   Carried to slice B:
   - doctor's lines in a bare repository and in an old layout;
   - doc_truth's ABSENT allowances and its FOREIGN .brokkr/ entry;
   - init writing the folder;
   - compile and recipes refusing an old layout;
   - the JournalArgs fold of the --realms/--db pairs.
   Carried as over-refusals with true text: Unwatched, TrackedSubmodule and Sparse. Decision 0083 ruling 4's example still shows the compile-derived moves the operator dropped: the operator's to amend.

This run lands one pull request under decision 0051, so the contribution gate can vouch for it.

For the implement phase only: if a finding returns the branch, fix exactly that finding and prove it with a test bound by a compiling mutation. Then run, all clean: cargo fmt --all -- --check; cargo clippy on the crates you touched, with -D warnings; typos --hidden; quality/ratchet.sh files, clones and api. If you change help text, leave docs/reference/cli.md and say so: the controller regenerates it, because your sandbox refuses the env-prefixed command. If a help edit re-keys clones, say so with the ratchet's output; the controller refreshes the baseline. A new test file is named *_tests.rs, or the exact-coverage gate counts it as production. Tests that drive a run through the CLI build their engine through tests/support/engine.rs.

Commit one signed-off commit ending "Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>", and never push. Do not run scripts/coverage-exact.sh; the controller runs it. Run every command in the foreground: never background a command or schedule a wakeup, because a headless seat ends when it waits.

Threat model (operator ruling, 2026-09-26): catch realistic accidental misuse, and fail closed on what cannot be read.
